{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Jacob saw that there was grain.</b> He heard that there was grain in Egypt, as it is written immediately afterward: 'Behold, I have heard that there is grain in Egypt.' Similarly: 'And all the people saw the voices.'" "<b>Why do you look.</b> Rashi explained: do not show yourselves. And so he explained in [the case of] the fast: they had much wheat, and went only for this reason — so as not to be seen before Yishmael and Esav, who are envious and hungry. And further, Rashi explained in the name of others: I have heard that it is an expression of wasting away — why should you grow gaunt with hunger. It is similar to: 'and he who waters — יורא — shall also be watered.' That is, the word תתראו and the word יורא are both written with alef, and that is the analogy — even though this is an expression of wasting away and that is an expression of satiation, we find many words whose root letters are identical but whose meanings are opposite to each other — such as דשן and לדשנו, שרש and תשרש, מחלצות and ואחלצה, לשבור — to break — and יוסף הוא המשביר — Yosef is the one who provides sustenance — and many more."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:26.741058375Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}